      "bbox": [
        351,
        91,
        456,
        915
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "• It features, as you will see, σ and α, just like the aorist indicative active\n(129–31). This would lead you to expect the active aorist optative end-\nings to be -σαιμι -σαις -σαι, and these do occur.\n• However, Greek prefers the alternatives using -ει- given in the conjuga-\ntion below:",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": "bullet",
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
